A||||8||PlasticWrapd||Cheap PROM upgrade for non-DIS 2.5||||10||
Z||000000||PlasticWrapd||11-30-2000||12:09 PM||||I discovered this when looking for a replacement PROM after using the "orange wire method" to clear the stored codes in the ECM (see previos post).<P>After toasting the PROM twice, I couldn't find another "Fiero" PROM.  Since I was in a bind, I got several different proms that are compatable with the 1226156 & 1226864 computers.  They all worked, but each had different problems such as poor performance and over-rich mixture, except one.  One prom actually improved throttle response and increased acceleration a bit.  The prom is from a 1985 1.8L OHC with TBI and 5 speed.  The engine code is "O" for this engine.  I can only say WOW! I can see no difference in mileage and the emissions "smell" normal, but it packs a little extra punch.  Give it a shot.  If you need the actual code on the PROM, I can take a look and post it here.||||reg||10
Z||000001||theogre||11-30-2000||08:11 PM||||Anyone playing with ECM's should go to <A HREF="http://www.diy-efi.org" TARGET=_blank>www.diy-efi.org</A>  an study the GM stuff carefully.<P>Those PROMs are not the only code stored in C3 ECMs. Some of it is in another ROM that you can't remove. You really want to make sure the PROM is from the same model ECM whenever posible. You want to be careful doing this. you could damage the engine with the wrong PROM.<P>You really want to have an ECM scanner when you do stuff like this. That can help you find out just what the PROM is doing. especially if it's not working right.<P>Anyone thinking of doing this to the DIS motor should read my cave notes on the ECM. It tells you why this won't always work for the 1227748 ECM. This kind of thing is actually easier to do with the DIS ecm once you know what the issues are. I'm presently investigating the use of non Fiero PROMs in this configuration. I'll post more info when I get it.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-30-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Uaana||11-30-2000||11:57 PM||||Didnt Cliff have a custom setup that was lurking in the unused areas of the prom?<BR>Think he posted being able to boost HP by about 10-15 ponies doing this simple upgrade.  ||||reg||5
Z||000003||theogre||12-01-2000||09:10 PM||||That was an april fools joke that even I fell for. (Way to much going on this year.... I need a computer just to know what day it is.)||||reg||1
Z||000004||horseman||12-03-2000||09:57 PM||||Hey Plas..,<BR>What is the number of the proms that you are using from the 1.8? Please post them or email me so that I can reference them.<P>Thanks in advance,<P>Charlie||||reg||14
Z||000005||horseman||12-06-2000||01:50 AM||||Any #'s for that prom and ecm yet Plas...?<BR>I am dying to try it.<BR>charlie||||reg||6
Z||000006||PlasticWrapd||12-06-2000||09:18 AM||||Dunno the prom numbers, a real pain pulling the console apart to check.  But, if I must....   Anyway I grabbed the whole computer out of a 1985 Buick.  Can't remember the model, but it's the size of a Sunbird.  The computer number is 1226864 (same circuit board as the 1226156 that came in the 84 Fiero).  All you really need is the year, engine size and code.  The proms should all contain the same code ( or code that's very close ).  Look for GM products from 1985 with the 1226864 computer.  The engine is a 1.8 FI OHC, and the engine code is "O".  Since my last post, I also advanced the static timing 2 degrees which helped even more. This is done with a timing light and the computer in diagnostic mode.||||reg||1
Z||000007||horseman||12-06-2000||01:22 PM||||Ok Plas..,<BR>I called the dealer Parts dept. I told him the eng. size,year,code,even the ecm #1226864.<BR>He said that there were 3 different proms for that ecm. Said that there should be a sticker or stamp on the ecm(Buick box). <BR>One is..FAM,  Two is FAN, three is FDM.<BR>Can you see which one is on the box that you pulled? Oh, and for reference sake, the model buick is a skyhawk(j-body). I had one years ago as a daily driver.<BR>Charlie||||reg||5
Z||000008||286SE'S||12-06-2000||02:32 PM||||There are lots of different proms. <BR>Different proms for different tires?! <BR>That is an eye-opener.<BR>Here is a handy chart:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.cruzers.com/~ludis/fieroprom.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cruzers.com/~ludis/fieroprom.html</A> ||||reg||1
